            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "patty"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I just want to say thanks SO much! I've been searching for this long lost treasure in my mum's old 'recipe box' (consisting of hundreds of loose paper bits and pieces!) My mum used to make this treat for us as kids almost every Sunday afternoon. She passed away many years ago, so I'd love to rekindle the old tradition with my sisters and the growing family!",
            "datePublished": "2011-08-30T13:42:17.300Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "lynnettemarie"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is the first \"sea foam\" candy recipe that I haven't burned BUT I don't really consider it a true sea foam. Its really more like divinity. I was a little disappointed because I wanted to make it for a gift for my sister in law, but this is NOT the sea foam candy that she loves so much. Thanks for sharing. Great recipe if you want something more like divinity.",
            "datePublished": "2010-12-18T11:54:17.840Z"
          },
          {
